{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E7DA1RKe9Dwau69ciRSq1h","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd101-install\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/install: Copy Files and Set Attributes\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD install that differs from GNU install in flag names and behavior.\n6\t  GNU install copies files while setting ownership, permissions, and optionally creating\n7\t  directories. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n8\t  (ginstall, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by\n9\t  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Copy files while setting ownership and permissions.\n13\t  - G2: Support directory creation mode.\n14\t  - G3: Support backup and stripping options.\n15\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against ginstall via differential testing.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: File installation\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: Must copy SOURCE to DEST, setting permissions to 755 by default (or as specified by -m).\n23\t      - R1.2:\n24\t          text: \"-m MODE or --mode=MODE must set the permission mode on the installed file (octal or symbolic).\"\n25\t      - R1.3:\n26\t          text: \"-o OWNER or --owner=OWNER must set the owner of the installed file.\"\n27\t      - R1.4:\n28\t          text: \"-g GROUP or --group=GROUP must set the group of the installed file.\"\n29\t\n30\t  R2:\n31\t    title: Directory creation and backup\n32\t    items:\n33\t      - R2.1:\n34\t          text: \"-d or --directory must create each given directory and any missing parent directories, like mkdir -p. No file copying is performed in this mode.\"\n35\t      - R2.2:\n36\t          text: \"-D must create all leading destination directory components, then copy SOURCE to DEST.\"\n37\t      - R2.3:\n38\t          text: \"-b or --backup must make a backup of each existing destination file. --suffix=SUFFIX sets the backup suffix (default ~).\"\n39\t      - R2.4:\n40\t          text: \"-v or --verbose must print the name of each file as it is installed.\"\n41\t\n42\t  R3:\n43\t    title: Comparison and exit codes\n44\t    items:\n45\t      - R3.1:\n46\t          text: \"-C or --compare must not install if the source and destination are identical (same content and permissions). This avoids updating timestamps unnecessarily.\"\n47\t      - R3.2:\n48\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are installed successfully. Must exit 1 on any error.\n49\t      - R3.3:\n50\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n51\t\n52\tnon_goals:\n53\t  - cmd/install does not implement --strip (binary stripping requires external strip tool).\n54\t  - cmd/install does not implement SELinux context setting.\n55\t\n56\tacceptance_criteria:\n57\t  - id: AC1\n58\t    criterion: \"install src dest copies src to dest with mode 755, matching ginstall.\"\n59\t    traces:\n60\t      - R1.1\n61\t  - id: AC2\n62\t    criterion: \"install -d dir1/dir2 creates directories, matching ginstall -d.\"\n63\t    traces:\n64\t      - R2.1\n65\t  - id: AC3\n66\t    criterion: \"install -m 644 src dest sets mode 644, matching ginstall.\"\n67\t    traces:\n68\t      - R1.2\n69\t  - id: AC4\n70\t    criterion: \"Differential test against ginstall passes.\"\n71\t    traces:\n72\t      - R1.1\n73\t      - R1.2\n74\t      - R2.1\n75\t  - id: AC5\n76\t    criterion: \"cmd/install compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n77\t    traces:\n78\t      - R1.1\n79\t      - R1.2\n80\t      - R1.3\n81\t      - R1.4\n82\t      - R2.1\n83\t      - R2.2\n84\t      - R2.3\n85\t      - R2.4\n86\t      - R3.1\n87\t      - R3.2\n88\t      - R3.3\n89\t\n90\tpackage_contract:\n91\t  imports:\n92\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"81dea4c7-429d-4c2f-9db0-26c45684447d","uuid":"9ffb6c6b-b58f-4aab-87ff-c50cfb1a41fa","timestamp":"2026-05-27T15:10:42.128Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5594/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd101-install.yaml","content":"id: srd101-install\ntitle: \"cmd/install: Copy Files and Set Attributes\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships a BSD install that differs from GNU install in flag names and behavior.\n  GNU install copies files while setting ownership, permissions, and optionally creating\n  directories. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n  (ginstall, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by\n  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Copy files while setting ownership and permissions.\n  - G2: Support directory creation mode.\n  - G3: Support backup and stripping options.\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against ginstall via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: File installation\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must copy SOURCE to DEST, setting permissions to 755 by default (or as specified by -m).\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"-m MODE or --mode=MODE must set the permission mode on the installed file (octal or symbolic).\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"-o OWNER or --owner=OWNER must set the owner of the installed file.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"-g GROUP or --group=GROUP must set the group of the installed file.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Directory creation and backup\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-d or --directory must create each given directory and any missing parent directories, like mkdir -p. No file copying is performed in this mode.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-D must create all leading destination directory components, then copy SOURCE to DEST.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-b or --backup must make a backup of each existing destination file. --suffix=SUFFIX sets the backup suffix (default ~).\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"-v or --verbose must print the name of each file as it is installed.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Comparison and exit codes\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-C or --compare must not install if the source and destination are identical (same content and permissions). This avoids updating timestamps unnecessarily.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are installed successfully. Must exit 1 on any error.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/install does not implement --strip (binary stripping requires external strip tool).\n  - cmd/install does not implement SELinux context setting.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"install src dest copies src to dest with mode 755, matching ginstall.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"install -d dir1/dir2 creates directories, matching ginstall -d.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"install -m 644 src dest sets mode 644, matching ginstall.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against ginstall passes.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/install compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":93,"startLine":1,"totalLines":93}}}
